{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "_purpose": "A BUILD RECORD: the individual upgrade components of one build, read from the donor car itself — the upgrade shop's INSTALLED tiles per category, the My Cars stats pane, and the tune menu's tab row (a locked downloaded tune still shows which tabs exist: Brakes tab = race brakes installed, Antiroll Bars tab = race ARBs, Differential tab = sport/race diff, Gearing tab = sport/race transmission, Aero tab = adjustable aero). Telemetry cannot name individual parts (many stacks give the same outputs) — it VERIFIES them: gear count vs transmission, boost vs aspiration, cyl/redline vs engine swap, drivetrain, exact PI, pane hp/tq/weight vs measured. File name: <ordinal>-<short-label>.json. Matched to a session car by 'cid' (ordinal|drivetrain|cyl|PI), optionally 'build_id'.",
